    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, I really do. Accuracy is important. But the reality is, we only hit a 5% increase in coral health with that last project, and our internal goal was 20%. If we just put \"5%\" in the application, the GEF is going to think we're ineffective and we'll lose the grant entirely. \n\nIs there really no way to frame that 5% so it sounds like a significant win? Like, maybe focusing on the resilience or the baseline difficulty? I'm not saying we lie about the number, but we have to make it sound like a major success or we're done for.",
